      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subjects offered in the academic year 2024: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- total of 12 units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- Mathematics department (Course 18): COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject code: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE\n- subject title: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- school name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- number of such subjects offered in that school: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE\n- variance of the total units of courses offered by that department: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- standard deviation of the total units of courses offered by that department: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- degree-granting departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- courses with a non-null total units value: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n\n## Join Keys\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and, for each school, the number of such subjects offered in that school (only including schools where at least 2 such subjects are offered), and also show the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses with a non-null total units value and only for degree-granting departments), and only include results where the department name and school name match in both sets of criteria. List the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, subject count, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units. Do not return any rounded answers."
