uniform row replication, so this join does not distort the statistics; it only requires the department to have at least one course-description row (Mathematics does, per dw_1393/dw_1049 precedents using SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION for Mathematics).\n- \"Number of such subjects offered in that school\": COUNT of SUBJECT_CODE per SCHOOL_NAME with HAVING ≥ 2 (dw_3904 precedent counts subject codes per school with COUNT(*)); \"at least 2\" → HAVING COUNT(...) >= 2.\n- \"Department name and school name match in both sets\" → inner join of the two sets on both DEPARTMENT_NAME and SCHOOL_NAME (dw_1471 joins its two subqueries on DEPARTMENT_NAME).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\ndw_1471 serves the exact question pattern (2024 12-unit Math subjects with school attribution + department unit dispersion appended per row). dw_3311/dw_2151/dw_1393/dw_1049 establish the VARIANCE/STDDEV-of-TOTAL_UNITS-per-degree-granting-department pattern.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (semantic_get full columns); column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, concept_department_dimension, concept_course_catalog_sources (semantic_get); CIS_COURSE_CATALOG neighbors (semantic_graph); metrics dw_1471, dw_3311, dw_2210, dw_3248, dw_1393, dw_1049, dw_1212, dw_2151, dw_3904 (semantic_get full SQL). mysql_query was attempted repeatedly but the database returned \"Access denied\" on every call, so data-level verification was not possible; the query is grounded in precedent SQL and documented join keys instead.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\nTwo CTEs joined at the end:\n1. **Subject set**: SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED on DEPARTMENT_CODE, filtered ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024, TOTAL_UNITS = 12, DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' (exactly as dw_1471).\n2. **School counts**: COUNT(SUBJECT_CODE) per SCHOOL_NAME over set 1, HAVING ≥ 2.\n3. **Department unit stats**: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE) ⋈ CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (DEPARTMENT_CODE), WHERE CIS TOTAL_UNITS IS NOT NULL AND IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y', grouped by DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, computing VARIANCE() and bare STDDEV().\n4. Final inner join on SCHOOL_NAME (set 1 ↔ counts) and on DEPARTMENT_NAME + SCHOOL_NAME (set 1 ↔ stats), selecting the seven requested columns in order, unrounded.\n\n",
